quinsock (0.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * No changes to the server itself.
  * Packages are now built on GitHub and published with each release, with a
    SHA256SUMS file whose names match the downloaded files.

 -- M. Aranovsky <m.aranovsky@igroshop.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 14:57:32 +0000

quinsock (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * CONNECT tries resolved addresses Happy Eyeballs style (RFC 8305), so a host
    with broken IPv6 no longer fails dual-stack destinations after connect_secs.
  * Raise the default DNS timeout to 15 s so a lost DNS packet is retried by the
    system resolver instead of failing the request.
  * Log failed CONNECT requests at info level.

 -- M. Aranovsky <m.aranovsky@igroshop.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:45:00 +0000

quinsock (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: SOCKS5 (RFC 1928) with CONNECT, BIND and UDP ASSOCIATE,
    RFC 1929 username/password authentication and a QUIC-tuned UDP relay.

 -- M. Aranovsky <m.aranovsky@igroshop.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
